## what is replica set
a replica set is a controller used by deployement that ensures the correct number of identical pods are running.
for example if a pod is determined to be unhealthy , a controller will terminate that pod. the replicaSet will 
detect that not unough pods for that application or worklods are running and will create another pods,
replica sets are also used to update and delete pods.

## What is a Deployment in Kubernetes..?
A Deployment is a Kubernetes resource that manages ReplicaSets and provides declarative updates for applications.
It ensures that the desired number of application Pods are running and provides features such as rolling updates, rollbacks and scaling.
Whenever we update the application configuration, such as changing the container image version, 
the Deployment creates a new ReplicaSet and gradually replaces the old Pods with new Pods without 
requiring us to manually delete and recreate them.
(vikas)additionally :- we can say deployments are sets of identical pods. the member of the set 
may change as some pods are terminated and others are started, but they are all running the same application.
the pods are running same application because they are created using the same pod template.

kubectl create deployment nginxdeploy  --image=nginx :- create deployment and pod as well.
kubectl get po :- get pod status.
kubectl delete po <podName> : delete pod
## deployment auto create new pod if a existing pod is deleted.

